- @page_title = "Terms of Use"

= render PageHeaderComponent.new(title: "Terms of Use", back_href: native_app? ? nil : today_path, back_label: "Back to today")

= render CardComponent.new(class: "p-6 mb-4") do
  .legal-copy
    %p.text-sm.text-text-secondary.mb-6
      Last updated 25 August 2026

    %h2 Tally is not medical advice
    %p
      Tally records what you tell it you ate and adds up the numbers. It is a
      notebook, not a clinician. Nothing in it is medical, nutritional or dietary
      advice, and it is not a substitute for a doctor or a registered dietitian.
      Talk to a qualified professional before changing what you eat, especially
      if you are pregnant, are managing a medical condition, or have a history of
      disordered eating.

    %h2 Nutrition numbers are estimates
    %p
      Calorie and macronutrient figures come from Open Food Facts, USDA
      FoodData Central, and foods entered by you. Open Food Facts is
      community-maintained, so entries can be incomplete or wrong, and
      manufacturers change recipes without changing barcodes. Treat every number
      as an approximation. If one looks wrong, it may well be — correct it by
      creating your own food entry.

    %h2 Your account
    %p
      Keep your password to yourself; you are responsible for what happens under
      your account. Give a real email address, because password resets go there.
      One person per account.

    %h2 Your content
    %p
      The foods, recipes and meal templates you create stay yours. Tally stores
      them to show them back to you and claims no ownership. They are visible only
      to you.

    %h2 Acceptable use
    %p
      Don't attack the service, scrape it, or use it to break the law. Tally's
      food searches ride on free public APIs, so automated bulk querying spoils
      it for everyone.

    %h2 Availability
    %p
      Tally is provided as-is, with no guarantee of uptime and no warranty. It is
      a small independent app, not an enterprise service. Keep your own record of
      anything you cannot afford to lose. To the extent the law allows, Tally's
      developer is not liable for losses arising from your use of the app.

    %h2 Ending things
    %p
      Delete your account whenever you like, from Settings → Delete account. It
      takes effect immediately and cannot be undone. Accounts used to abuse the
      service may be suspended.

    %h2 Changes
    %p
      These terms may change; the date at the top will say when. Continuing to
      use Tally after a change means accepting it.

    %h2 Contact
    %p
      Questions go to
      = succeed "." do
        %a.text-primary.underline{href: "mailto:hello@tally.quest"} hello@tally.quest
